<div class="columnArticleClass two-layout-bg-white" id="twoColumnArticleTheme"><div id="sectionHeadingForTwoColumnArticle"><div class="section-heading mb-4 container text-start" data-ste-element="Sites: Section Heading"><div><div class="row text-start"><div class="col col-md-8"><h2 class="header-focus"><span>Why Substation automation unit?</span></h2></div></div></div></div></div><div class="text-start container multitextblock two-column-article"><div class="m-t-xl two-column-article-content layout-1-to-1 two-layout-top-alignment"><div class="p-lg-r-lg"><div><p>The SICAM A8000 is a substation automation unit designed to automate widely distributed processes across the energy chain. Its powerful dual-core CPU combines different communication protocols on a single interface, significantly reducing hardware requirements and engineering costs. It is the first system to allow other applications to be loaded onto the same device using docker container technology.</p></div></div><div><div><div><div class="mb-4"><div class="p-0 col-sm-12 m-auto ratio ratio-16x9"><disw-video videoid="5caa89aa-dfa9-4c3b-87e2-9b8488c1f99b" locale="en-US" autoplay="false"></disw-video></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div id='5KJAu0FnzyKIiMwoaawMl7' class='sitesThreeColTiles themed-component-wrapper' data-ste-section='three-col-tiles_3' data-ste-section-id='5KJAu0FnzyKIiMwoaawMl7'>
